  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "If the following three linear equations have a non-trivial solution, then\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{array}{l}\r\nx+4 a y+a z=0 \\\\\r\nx+3 b y+b z=0 \\\\\r\nx+2 c y+c z=0\r\n\\end{array}\r\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "U97kp",
      "text": "$a, b, c$ are in $A P$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "9ovCW",
      "text": "$a, b, c$ are in $G$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Y9h4f",
      "text": "$a, b, c$ are in $\\mathrm{HP}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Q4QJz",
      "text": "$a+b+c=0$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "For non-trivial solution, We have, $\\left|\\begin{array}{ccc}1 & 4 a & a \\\\ 1 & 3 b & b \\\\ 1 & 2 c & c\\end{array}\\right|=0$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad 1(3 b c-2 b c)-(4 a c-2 a c)+1(4 a b-3 a b)=0$\r\n$\\Rightarrow b c-2 a c+a b=0$\r\n$\\Rightarrow b c+a b=2 a c$\r\n$\\Rightarrow b(a+c)=2 a c$\r\n$\\Rightarrow b=\\frac{2 a c}{a+c}$\r\n$\\Rightarrow a, b, c$ are in $\\mathrm{HP}$",
    "image": null
  },
